  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-15T15:12:47.690Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I was in the middle of debugging my Udon code and I wanted to test it in an actual room instead of the local test world, so I uploaded it as a private world and joined it on both clients. One of them (the master) got kicked for being a duplicate, and the game got stuck on a black screen after that.\nI tried twice and the issue happened the exact same way both times. I only tested on desktop.\nSteps:\n- Launch 2 clients using the SDK into a local world\n- On client 1, open the menu and join a regular, remote world (I used invite only)\n- On vrchat.com/home, send yourself an invite to the instance from the link on the left under your profile\n- On client 2, accept the self-invite\n- Client 1 will get kicked\n- On client 1, click \"okay\"\n- Client 1 should now be stuck on a black screen, with the only way to exit it is to press ALT+TAB and close the window",
